# Frontend vs backend folders

This repo is two apps. Never mix them.

- `frontend/` — Vite + React UI (components, hooks, pages, browser libs like `xlsx`)
- `backend/` — Express + MongoDB API (routes, database, uploads, PDF parsing)

## Do

- Put UI/browser packages in `frontend/package.json`
- Put server packages in `backend/package.json`
- Call the API from `frontend/src/api` with `/api/...` paths
- Spreadsheet parsing (`xlsx`) stays in `frontend/` — it runs in the browser

## Don't

- Don't run `vite` or `npm run dev` on Render. Build the UI, then start Express (`npm start`)
- Don't import React, Vite, or `xlsx` from `backend/`
- Don't put Express routes or MongoDB access in `frontend/`
- Don't install frontend deps at the repo root

## Render

- Build: `npm run build` (installs both apps, writes `frontend/dist`)
- Start: `npm start` (Express serves `/api` and the built UI)
